Describe a rule that is important in your school or work
- what the rule is
- if the people break this rule, what will happen
- why do you think this is an important rule

One of the most important rules both at my workplace and during my school years is punctuality. The rule is quite simple: everyone is expected to arrive on time for work or class.

If people break this rule repeatedly, there can be several consequences. In the workplace, being late too often may affect a person’s professional image, lead to warnings from managers, or even result in losing their job in serious cases. At school, students who arrive late may interrupt the lesson, miss important information, or receive penalties such as losing attendance marks.

I believe this is an important rule because it shows respect for other people’s time and helps everything run more smoothly and efficiently. For example, if one person is late during a meeting or class, it can delay the entire schedule and affect everyone else.

In addition, punctuality helps people develop discipline and responsibility, which are valuable qualities not only in school or at work but also in everyday life. I also think being on time creates a positive impression and shows that a person is reliable and professional.

Overall, punctuality may seem like a small thing, but it plays a very important role in maintaining an organized and productive environment.
